ll narrow bill with a slight hooked tip, and a short rounded tail; unmistakably a shearwater, not a pigeon, albatross or fork-tailed tern. Calm Atlantic water stretches behind the ivory-and-sage coastal slope, the bird and burrow are the single clear homecoming story. One bird only, natural wing anatomy and proportions. Do not place a letter already at the burrow, since the letter arrived later. Do not show a globe route, a compass icon, magnetic field lines, glowing eyes or a proven protein mechanism. This depicts the observed return, while the mechanism of knowing its location remains unresolved. Soft feather detail, sage sea, ivory sky, minimal terracotta coastal stones.",
